From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:19:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: x1e80100: Enable dual edge errata

It has been observed that dual edge triggered wakeirq GPIOs on X1E80100
don't trigger interrupts on the falling edge, now that its GPIO
interrupts go through the PDC.

Enabling wakeirq_dual_edge_errata for X1E80100 indicates that its PDC
suffers from the same problem described, and worked around, in
c3c0c2e18d94 ("pinctrl: qcom: Handle broken/missing PDC dual edge IRQs
on sc7180"), so enable the workaround for X1E80100 as well.

The specific problem seen without this is that gpio-keys only ever sees
the first edge of the lid GPIO (TLMM 92) on the ASUS Zenbook 14
(UX3480QA): the lid interrupt fires once after boot and never again, so
closing the lid neither reports the switch nor suspends. With the
workaround both edges arrive and the lid suspends and resumes the
machine.

Fixes: 77fbc756d9cb ("Revert \"pinctrl: qcom: x1e80100: Bypass PDC wakeup parent for now\"")
Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c
index e4c0abc..b4e7941 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-x1e80100.c
@@ -1837,6 +1837,7 @@ static const struct msm_pinctrl_soc_data x1e80100_pinctrl = {
 	.ngpios = 239,
 	.wakeirq_map = x1e80100_pdc_map,
 	.nwakeirq_map = ARRAY_SIZE(x1e80100_pdc_map),
+	.wakeirq_dual_edge_errata = true,
 	.egpio_func = 9,
 };
 
